    <!--
      `Track Info` and `Controls`, anchored absolutely rather than stacked.

      The frozen boxes are 24 and 18 tall against line heights of 24 and 18 - a box
      exactly as tall as its own font size. Figma can draw that because it has no
      font padding and honours the declared line height literally; Android cannot,
      because Montserrat Black at 24sp needs about 29dp of ascent-to-descent and
      Regular at 18sp about 22dp. Forcing the frozen heights would clip the glyphs,
      which is the defect class this migration does not reproduce.

      So each block keeps a safe, natural height and is positioned by its own
      offset from the page top. The blocks grow inwards into the frozen 8 gap
      instead of pushing everything below them down, which is what keeps the
      controls - and the section as a whole - exactly where the frozen frame puts
      them. Measured, the visible gap between the two lines of text comes out at
      about 7 against the frozen 8.
    -->
    <!--
      The title is anchored by its BOTTOM, just above the artist, so a two-line
      title grows up into the gap under the artwork instead of over the artist.
      See fragment_myata_stream.xml for the measurements behind that.

      3dp is what the frozen offsets leave between the two boxes in practice: the
      frozen title box is 24 tall against a 292 top and a 324 artist, which is an
      8 gap, and Android's real box is 29.3 because Montserrat Black at 24sp does
      not fit in 24. The 8 absorbs the difference and 3 is what is left. Keeping
      the gap rather than a second absolute offset is what ties the title to the
      artist, so the frozen 292 falls out of it: 324 - 3 - 29.3 = 291.7.
    -->
    <dimen name="player_track_title_artist_gap">3dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_track_artist_top">324dp</dimen>

