    <!--
      The nominal size of the two play/pause glyphs.

      One dimen for both, by the owner's requirement that the pair share a size,
      and because a pair that can drift apart eventually does. 48 is an official
      Material size, and it is the size at which Material's pause ink (28.0dp)
      lands within 2% of what the superseded owner-final pause painted (27.33dp),
      so the control kept its weight across the swap.

      The glyphs are drawn by scaleType=center inside the 80x80 button, so this
      is the whole of their placement: no offset, no scale, nothing per-glyph.
      What each one paints inside its 48 box is a property of the official path
      and is not set anywhere - see ic_player_play.xml. Measured at this size:

        play    405/960 x 494/960 of 48  ->  20.25 x 24.70,  box +2.125 right
        pause   560/960, both axes       ->  28.00 x 28.00,  box centred

      Play's +2.125 is Google's own optical correction, not something applied
      here: it is what puts the triangle's visual mass on the control centre.
      PlayerControlRenderTest rasterises the control and measures both boxes.
    -->
    <dimen name="player_play_glyph_size">48dp</dimen>
    <!--
      The connecting indicator, which does need a dimen of its own because it is
      a real view rather than a path.

      It is deliberately unchanged by the glyph swap. It stands in for the glyph
      rather than copying it, the design has nothing to say about a connecting
      state, and 27.33 sits between the new pair's 20.25 and 28.00 - so the
      control reads the same size through play -> connecting -> pause, which is
      the only thing this number has ever had to do.
    -->
    <dimen name="player_play_icon">27.33dp</dimen>
    <!--
      The connecting indicator's own geometry.

      Thickness is the point of these: the Material FILL 0 glyphs paint a 3.97dp
      wall, the platform's indeterminate drawable painted 2.17dp, and the
      indicator stands in for the glyph so it has to carry the glyph's weight. 4
      is that wall, to the nearest whole dp.

      Diameter is what must NOT change, so it is the diameter the platform
      drawable painted, kept: its vector is a radius-18 circle with a 4-wide
      stroke in a 48 viewport, drawn into player_play_icon's 27.33 box, so the
      outer diameter was 2 x (18 + 2) x 27.33/48 = 22.78. Measured off the
      screen before the swap: 22.75.

      The inset exists to stop the drawable being rescaled. CircularDrawingDelegate
      scales its canvas by bounds/preferred size, so the two have to agree or the
      thickness above is not the thickness painted: inset is therefore whatever
      makes the indicator's preferred size come to player_play_icon exactly.
      PlayerControlRenderTest measures the painted stroke, so a Material release
      that redefines how preferred size is composed fails there rather than
      silently re-scaling this.
    -->
    <dimen name="player_play_spinner_diameter">22.78dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_play_spinner_thickness">4dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_play_spinner_inset">2.275dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_action_width">49dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_action_height">54dp</dimen>
